1004:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/object/trendlog.c **** /****************************************************************************
1005:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/object/trendlog.c ****  * Build a list of Trend Log entries from the Log Buffer property as        *
1006:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/object/trendlog.c ****  * required for the ReadsRange functionality.                               *
1007:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/object/trendlog.c ****  *                                                                          *
1008:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/object/trendlog.c ****  * We have to support By Position, By Sequence and By Time requests.        *
1009:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/object/trendlog.c ****  *                                                                          *
1010:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/object/trendlog.c ****  * We do assume the list cannot change whilst we are accessing it so would  *
1011:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/object/trendlog.c ****  * not be multithread safe if there are other tasks that write to the log.  *
1012:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/object/trendlog.c ****  *                                                                          *
1013:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/object/trendlog.c ****  * We take the simple approach here to filling the buffer by taking a max   *
1014:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/object/trendlog.c ****  * size for a single entry and then stopping if there is less than that     *
1015:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/object/trendlog.c ****  * left in the buffer. You could build each entry in a seperate buffer and  *
1016:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/object/trendlog.c ****  * determine the exact length before copying but this is time consuming,    *
1017:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/object/trendlog.c ****  * requires more memory and would probably only let you sqeeeze one more    *
1018:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/object/trendlog.c ****  * entry in on occasion. The value is calculated as 10 bytes for the time   *
1019:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/object/trendlog.c ****  * stamp + 6 bytes for our largest data item (bit string capped at 32 bits) *
1020:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/object/trendlog.c ****  * + 3 bytes for the status flags + 4 for the context tags to give 23.      *
1021:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/object/trendlog.c ****  ****************************************************************************/
1022:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/object/trendlog.c **** 
1023:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/object/trendlog.c **** #define TL_MAX_ENC 23   /* Maximum size of encoded log entry, see above */
